winewayland: publish an unmeasured output's work area before a maximized window follows onto it

Seen in the lab (regress182 agent, 11-05; he asked for it to be chased): on a mixed-scale desk (175% primary with a
top panel, 200% screen beside it without one), Photoshop 2026 maximized and moved to the 200% screen (Super+Shift+Right),
started there, or maximized and placed there by KWin, showed its MENU BAR ABOVE the top of the screen and a black strip
about 33 logical px tall at the bottom. Identical on 181 and 182c.

Mechanism (SOLID, lab desk p, winfo probe in a PMv2 view + neutron-follow log lines):
- Wayland has no work-area protocol. display.c gives an output its measured maximized height once something was
  maximized on it in this prefix (.neutron-maximized-inset), else the 32-logical-px titlebar estimate. A fresh Photoshop
  prefix has no line for the 200% screen, so its rcWork was (3841,228)-(7681,2324) on monitor (3841,164)-(7681,2324):
  64 raw px inset on a screen with no panel.
- wayland_window_follow_output moved the window to that rcWork: (3841,228)-(7681,2388), 64 px past the bottom. The same
  call reported the compositor's 1920x1080 configure as that output's measurement, but by PostMessage: the desktop
  process published the real work area only after the move.
- Photoshop reads its monitor's work area while handling the move: its maximized client (3841,164) came out 64 px ABOVE
  its window and its window region (which hides what lies outside the work area) ended at 2095. The menu bar (child
  OWL.ApplicationBar) fell outside the window's surface; the window's last 64 rows were black.
- Placing the window from the measurement alone (v1 of this patch) fixed the rect but not the picture: Photoshop still
  read the estimate and its window region came out (0,63)-(3840,2159) -- the menu-bar row black; RedrawWindow did not
  paint it.

Windows: the work area of the monitor a maximized window moves to is known before the move, so the window rect, the
app's client/region and the monitor list agree.

Fix: when the work area this maximized configure gives the output (display.c's rule and plausibility guard) differs
from the published rcWork, deliver the measurement synchronously (wayland_report_output_maximized_h_sync:
SendMessageTimeout to the desktop window, 1 s, SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG), so the monitor list is rebuilt BEFORE the move, then
move into the re-read work area; on a timeout still place the window from the measurement. Only a maximized (not
fullscreen) follow move onto another output, only when the configure belongs to that output (fits, same scale = what
workarea#3 records). Logs "neutron-follow-workarea:" when it acts.

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-182p = 182c + this winewayland.so, both arms on the same build, V1 unmeasured each run):
- maximized + Super+Shift+Right: ON 2/2 correct, OFF 2/2 bug (rect (3841,228)-(7681,2388), 65 px bottom strip).
- started with the pointer on V1 (KWin places it there): ON 2/2 correct, OFF 2/2 bug.
- restored, Super+PageUp, KWin maximizes it onto V1: ON 2/2 correct, OFF 2/2 bug.
- ON: "published synchronously: yes" every time; win = client = (3841,164)-(7681,2324), region (0,-1)-(3840,2159);
  both doc-move captures PIXEL-IDENTICAL (0 px) to regress182's known-good (V1 already measured) capture.
- Single 175% screen (Virtual-1 disabled): PS ON vs OFF pixel-identical (0 px), n=1 each.
- Lightroom Classic maximized + Super+Shift+Right to V1 (V1 unmeasured): OFF rect (3841,228)-(7681,2388), ON
  (3841,164)-(7681,2324); the window looks the same in both (title, menu, filmstrip in place), n=1 each.

Not covered: a window maximized by win32u directly on an unmeasured output without a follow move (no such path found;
restored Super+Shift+Right does not move Photoshop in KWin); Premiere was not moved to V1 in this rig (title drag
did nothing), so it is untested here (the change only acts on maximized follow moves); the WM_DPICHANGED suggested rect
is scaled twice when the new rect is already sized for the new output (seen, not changed here).

Kill switch: NEUTRON_FOLLOW_WORKAREA=0.


--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/waylanddrv.h
@@ -608,6 +608,7 @@
 static inline void neutron_zorder_changed(void) { InterlockedIncrement(&neutron_zorder_generation); }
 BOOL neutron_workarea_save_output(const char *name, int logical_h);
 void wayland_report_output_maximized_h(uint32_t output_id, int logical_h);
+BOOL wayland_report_output_maximized_h_sync(uint32_t output_id, int logical_h);
 BOOL wayland_surface_config_is_compatible(struct wayland_surface_config *conf,
                                           int width, int height,
                                           enum wayland_surface_config_state state);
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_output.c
@@ -167,6 +167,22 @@
     NtUserPostMessage(desktop_hwnd, WM_WAYLAND_INIT_DISPLAY_DEVICES, (WPARAM)logical_h, (LPARAM)output_id);
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON follow-workarea: the same report, delivered SYNCHRONOUSLY (bounded wait), for a maximized window that is about
+ * to move onto that output: when the call returns the desktop process has stored the measurement and rebuilt the
+ * monitor list, so this process -- and the application, while it handles the move -- reads the output's real work
+ * area instead of the estimate the measurement replaces. TRUE if the desktop process handled the message. */
+BOOL wayland_report_output_maximized_h_sync(uint32_t output_id, int logical_h)
+{
+    struct send_message_timeout_params params = {.flags = SMTO_ABORTIFHUNG, .timeout = 1000};
+    HWND desktop_hwnd;
+
+    if (!process_wayland.initialized || !output_id || logical_h <= 0 || !neutron_workarea_per_output()) return FALSE;
+    if (!(desktop_hwnd = NtUserGetDesktopWindow())) return FALSE;
+    NtUserMessageCall(desktop_hwnd, WM_WAYLAND_INIT_DISPLAY_DEVICES, (WPARAM)logical_h, (LPARAM)output_id, &params,
+                      NtUserSendMessageTimeout, FALSE);
+    return params.result != 0;
+}
+
 void wayland_report_maximized_logical_h(int logical_h)
 {
     HWND desktop_hwnd;
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -2034,6 +2034,14 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON follow-workarea: kill switch NEUTRON_FOLLOW_WORKAREA=0 (move to the monitor list's work area, as before). */
+static BOOL neutron_follow_workarea(void)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    if (on < 0) on = neutron_gate("NEUTRON_FOLLOW_WORKAREA", TRUE);
+    return on;
+}
+
 static void wayland_window_follow_output(HWND hwnd)
 {
     struct wayland_win_data *data;
@@ -2054,6 +2062,8 @@
     HMONITOR win_mon = 0, out_mon = 0;
     MONITORINFO win_mi = {.cbSize = sizeof(win_mi)}, out_mi = {.cbSize = sizeof(out_mi)};
     UINT context;
+    /* NEUTRON follow-workarea: the maximized configure is this output's (what workarea#3 records) */
+    BOOL cfg_for_output = FALSE;
 
     if (!(data = wayland_win_data_get(hwnd))) return;
     if ((surface = data->wayland_surface) && wayland_surface_is_toplevel(surface) &&
@@ -2119,6 +2129,7 @@
     {
         BOOL fits = !found || out_lw <= 0 || out_lh <= 0 || (cfg_w <= out_lw + 1 && cfg_h <= out_lh + 1);
         BOOL same_scale = !found || pref_scale <= 0.0 || out_scale <= 0.0 || fabs(pref_scale - out_scale) < 0.01;
+        cfg_for_output = found && cfg_h > 0 && fits && same_scale;
         if (!neutron_workarea_guard() || (fits && same_scale))
             wayland_report_output_maximized_h(id, cfg_h);
         else if (neutron_wl_diag())
@@ -2140,6 +2151,43 @@
 
         cur_area = full ? win_mi.rcMonitor : win_mi.rcWork;
         out_area = full ? out_mi.rcMonitor : out_mi.rcWork;
+        /* NEUTRON follow-workarea (2026-11-05). Lab desk: Photoshop 2026 maximized and moved to the 200% screen beside
+         * the 175% one (Super+Shift+Right), or started there: its menu bar sat above the top of the screen and a black
+         * strip about 33 logical px tall showed at the bottom. That screen has no panel, but until something has been
+         * maximized on it in this prefix its work area is the 32-logical-px titlebar estimate (display.c), so this
+         * move put the window at work top = monitor top + 64 px with the configure's full monitor height: 64 px past
+         * the bottom. The configure is that output's measurement, reported just above, but by message: the desktop
+         * process published the real work area (the monitor) only AFTER the move. Photoshop reads its monitor's work
+         * area while it handles the move -- its maximized client and its window region (which hides what lies outside
+         * the work area) come from it -- so it laid its client out 64 px ABOVE its own window: the menu bar fell
+         * outside the window's surface and the window's last 64 rows were non-client black. Placing the window from
+         * the measurement alone was not enough: Photoshop still read the estimate and its window region cut off the
+         * top 63 rows (black where the menu bar belongs). On Windows the work area of the monitor a maximized window
+         * moves to is known before the move, so the window, the app and the monitor list always agree. Do the same:
+         * when the work area this configure gives the output (display.c's rule) differs from the published one,
+         * deliver the measurement synchronously, so the monitor list is rebuilt BEFORE the move, then move into the
+         * re-read work area; if the desktop process does not answer in time, still place the window from the
+         * measurement. Kill switch NEUTRON_FOLLOW_WORKAREA=0. */
+        if (!full && cfg_for_output && neutron_follow_workarea() && neutron_workarea_per_output() &&
+            out_lh > 0 && cfg_h <= out_lh && (out_lh - cfg_h) < out_lh / 4)
+        {
+            RECT measured = out_mi.rcMonitor, published = out_area;
+            int mon_h = measured.bottom - measured.top;
+            int inset = (int)(((double)(out_lh - cfg_h) * mon_h) / out_lh + 0.5);
+            BOOL sent = FALSE;
+
+            if (inset > 0 && inset < mon_h) measured.top += inset;
+            if (!EqualRect(&measured, &out_area))
+            {
+                sent = wayland_report_output_maximized_h_sync(id, cfg_h);
+                if (sent && NtUserGetMonitorInfo(out_mon, &out_mi)) out_area = out_mi.rcWork;
+                ERR("neutron-follow-workarea: hwnd=%p output %u work area %s, configure %dx%d of %dx%d gives %s;"
+                    " published synchronously: %s, now %s\n", hwnd, id, wine_dbgstr_rect(&published), cfg_w, cfg_h,
+                    out_lw, out_lh, wine_dbgstr_rect(&measured), sent ? "yes" : "NO (timeout)",
+                    wine_dbgstr_rect(&out_area));
+            }
+            out_area = measured;
+        }
         left = cur_area.left - win.left;
         top = cur_area.top - win.top;
         right = win.right - cur_area.right;
